# Derived by hand from D6 as ruled (each entry of an unbounded function a cycle) and Type System ch. 4 (lifting over `?`): with 1, Work and both Incs are entered, three cycles, and 1 + 1 + 1 is 3; with 0, only Work is entered, and both lifted calls are `nil` at once.
test present

tick 0
  added:
    1: Ui.Label(text="working")

compute until idle: 3 ticks, 1 to 3

tick 3
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="3")

test absent

tick 0
  added:
    1: Ui.Label(text="working")

compute until idle: 1 tick, 1 to 1

tick 1
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="none")
